      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROCKS OR DIAMONDS (8) made late ground two back to finish just over a length from the winner over 1200m at Kembla. Thrown in the deep end last start and did a fair job to come from last and finish a distant sixth in the $1 million Callander-Presnell over the Randwick mile. Will appreciate the extra 200m in far weaker company. Winning hope. Stablemate DANCE WITH DESTINY (3) made late inroads to get up for third last time out over 1600m at Kembla, her second minor placing from as many runs this prep. Ready to peak at the third run back. WHAT SHE'S HAVING (6) has tackled a couple of maidens such as this recently and been competitive on each occasion. Deep into the prep and the form is holding up. Each-way hope. MOON FLASH (5) led and just failed to hold on in a game performance over the mile at Kembla last start. Capable of running another cheeky race. SPALPEEN (9) was utterly outclassed last start in the Callender-Presnell. Top four hope in this company.",
